    "text": "In this micro lesson, you will learn why matrices matter in AI images. A photo looks visual to us, but a computer can break it into tiny pixels. In grayscale, each pixel becomes one brightness number. Put those numbers in rows and columns, and you get a matrix. Color images use three number grids: red, green, and blue. AI scans these grids to find edges, shapes, and patterns. Remember: an image is a grid of numbers.",
